course: dictionary
lesson: 82
title: Activist: a word for people who push for change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An activist is a person who works hard to bring about political or social change. Read the words around the word to check its meaning. Activists campaign, protest or write letters to make people notice a problem and try to fix it.
explain: Look at the names in the lessons: Rosa Parks, Malala Yousafzai and Greta Thunberg are often described as activists. Each one spoke up for something she believed was important. Activists can be young or old, and they can work for any cause.
explain: «Some say young activists are told what to say by adults; others say young people think for themselves; both can be partly true.» The sentence does not tell you who is right. It shows that people disagree, so a good reader keeps an open mind.
fact: An activist is a person who works hard to bring about political or social change.
fact: Activists may campaign, protest or write letters to get people to take notice.
fact: Phrases show the cause: climate activist, civil rights activist and human rights activist.
fact: «Activists» is the plural, meaning more than one activist.
fact: Rosa Parks, Malala Yousafzai and Greta Thunberg are often named as activists.
exercise: «Some say young activists are told what to say by adults; others say young people think for themselves.» What does activist mean? | *A person who works hard to bring about change | A person who writes music for films | A person who sells goods at a market | A young person who plays a sport
exercise: Which job is most like an activist's work? | *Campaigning for cleaner rivers | Selling tickets at a cinema | Fishing from a boat | Painting a picture of a river
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Some say young activists are told what to say by adults» that tells you the activists are not grown up. | activists | say | adults | *young
test: Which phrase names an activist who campaigns about the environment? | *climate activist | human rights dinner | civil rights bridge
test: Greta Thunberg is often described as an activist. Why? | She is a famous singer | She runs a shop in town | She teaches at a school | *She campaigns to change how people treat the climate
exam: «Some say young activists are told what to say by adults; others say young people think for themselves; both can be partly true.» What does this sentence show? | *People disagree about whether young activists think for themselves | Everyone agrees that activists are always right | Young people cannot campaign for anything | Activists never speak in public
